WEBVTT

00:00:00.103 --> 00:00:06.173
The NULL checkpoint reviews one of the most
practical lessons in the module NOT

00:00:06.186 --> 00:00:11.970
IN can behave unexpectedly when NULL appears in the
returned set NOT

00:00:11.983 --> 00:00:18.013
EXISTS tests whether a matching row exists and
avoids that classic issue NOT

00:00:18.040 --> 00:00:23.687
IN is not always wrong The important point is that
you must understand

00:00:23.700 --> 00:00:26.332
the possible NULL values before relying on it
